d  before that Logan was the perfect send  off and his goodbye to the character  Wolverine  now it is also important to note that  Patrick Stewart also said the same exact  thing but he has recently met with  Marvel Studios President Kevin Feige to  talk about Charles Xavier and the MCU  now it seems kind of clear that Patrick  Stewart is done but perhaps he could be  brought on board to consult for the new  Professor Xavier that is coming on  because clearly Kevin Feige talked to  him about plans Patrick Stewart said it  himself and if he's not returning what  she stated what else could he be doing  meeting with Kevin Feige he's giving  advice on the character he's helping  Kevin Feige with the direction and it  does seem like Professor Xavier is going  to be headed to the MCU before Wolverine  does but when that time comes  when Wolverine enters the MCU they will  most likely speak to Hugh Jackman about  the character  about the direction they want to go  about the stories they want to tell  because he was a great Wolverine we all  loved him and it's hard to imagine  anybody else's Wolverine right now and I  think that the saddest thing is about  this all is that he said if it was seven  years ago and this had happened Disney  had bought Fox he would have loved to do  it he would have loved to play Wolverine  in the Marvel Cinematic Universe seven  years ago not even like a full ten years  but only seven years ago and he would  have done it we missed him just barely  but hopefully he does come back and  consult with Marvel Studios about what  to do with the next Wolverine that's  going to enter the MCU but this does  leave us with the question of if we do  get a Hulk vs. Wolverine movie who is  going to play Wolverine which of course  we can't answer right now there's no way  of knowing and what direction are they  going to take the Hulk  well according to the same report that  Mikey stated way back in September we  are going to get some version of  immortal Hulk 